        "original_id": "f8f965ce-df7c-50ce-a09d-c3befd03152a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stuart Hamblen, Shakin' Stevens, Michael Barratt\n- Works: \"This Ole House\" / \"This Old House\"\n- Topics: song publishing, UK music charts, recording career, commercial success\n\nFacts:\n- Stuart Hamblen wrote the popular song \"This Ole House,\" sometimes written \"This Old House,\" and the song was published in 1954.\n- Michael Barratt was born on 4 March 1948 and is known professionally as Shakin' Stevens.\n- Shakin' Stevens began his recording and performing career in the late 1960s.\n- Shakin' Stevens' commercial success began in 1980.\n- In 1981, Shakin' Stevens' recording of \"This Ole House\" topped the UK chart again.\n- Shakin' Stevens is a platinum-selling British rock and roll singer and songwriter.\n- Shakin' Stevens was the UK's biggest-selling singles artist of the 1980s.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4541c6ff-2eef-5e0f-8446-32e289e6e403",
        "text": "Page: This Ole House. Sentence: \"This Ole House\" (sometimes written \"This Old House\") is a popular song written by Stuart Hamblen, and published in 1954.\nPage: This Ole House. Sentence: The song again topped the UK chart in 1981 in a recording by Shakin' Stevens.\nPage: Shakin' Stevens. Sentence: Michael Barratt (born 4 March 1948), known as Shakin' Stevens, is a platinum-selling British rock and roll singer and songwriter who was the UK's biggest-selling singles artist of the 1980s.\nPage: Shakin' Stevens. Sentence: His recording and performing career began in the late 1960s, although it was not until 1980 that his commercial success began.",
